  "description": "The County Line is our all-road bike, designed around a 38mm tire with clearance up to 42mm. It fills the space between a dedicated road bike and today’s big-tire gravel bikes, built for the kind of riding we know well in Steamboat: pavement, smooth county-road gravel, and long days that move naturally between the two. The geometry leans more stable than a traditional road bike, adding confidence on dirt and rough pavement without losing the speed and efficiency that make it feel at home on the road.\nA 45mm road chainline and compatibility with both 1x and 2x drivetrains let the County Line be built toward fast road riding or a more mixed-surface setup. A new Moots carbon all-road fork brings fully integrated brake routing through our Ti stem, while in-house titanium UDH dropouts add modern drivetrain compatibility to a clean, durable platform.\nA road bike for routes that don’t stay paved.",
